redirectToRoute("hw_detail") does not work when I hit enter after the GET is being accepted by Nginx. When you hit enter after the GET request is being accepted by Nginx in Symfony (or an equivalent framework), the router might not be processing the redirect correctly. This is because the redirect is being triggered by the form submission or some other event, and hitting enter doesn't trigger the same mechanism.

To resolve this issue, you can make sure that the redirect is triggered by a proper form submission or event listener. One solution is to use a listener that reacts to the submit event of the form.

Here is an example of how to use a form event listener to trigger a redirect:

```php
// app/config/config.yml
form_events:
    form.validate: 'FOS\UserBundle\Form\Type\RegistrationFormType'
    form.post_success: 'fos_user_security_check'

// app/src/FOS/UserBundle/EventListener/SecurityCheckListener.php
<?php
namespace app\FOS\UserBundle\EventListener;
use FOS\UserBundle\Event\FormEvent;
use FOS\UserBundle\Model\UserInterface;
use Symfony\Component\HttpFoundation\RedirectResponse;
use Symfony\Component\Routing\RouterInterface;
use Symfony\Component\HttpKernel\HttpKernelInterface;

class SecurityCheckListener
{
    private $router;

    public function __construct(RouterInterface $router)
    {
        $this->router = $router;
    }

    public function onFormPostSuccess(FormEvent $event)
    {
        $request = $event->getRequest();
        $user = $event->getResolvedForm();

        // Check if the request is POST and the request method is POST
        if (HttpKernelInterface::MASTER_REQUEST === $request->getRequestMethod() && $request->getMethod() == 'POST') {
            // Process the user form data and set the user object in the event
            $address = $request->request->get('address');
            $rfid = $request->request->get('rfid');
            $token = $request->request->get('token');
            $event->setUser(new UserInterface($address, $rfid, $token));
        }
    }
}
```

